#
# example-restart-myapp@.service: AN EXAMPLE, the service half of example-restart-myapp.socket, which says why and how.
# One connection runs it once: it restarts myapp.service and nothing else. The connection is its standard input, and
# it reads nothing from it, so the client chooses neither the verb nor the unit; the instance name (the connection's
# number) appears nowhere in the command. The connection closes when the restart has finished, so the client sends
# nothing and reads to end of file to wait for it (a byte it sent is never read, and the close then resets the
# connection instead). systemctl's output goes to the journal, not to the client.

[Unit]
Description=Restart myapp.service for a governed agent (example)
CollectMode=inactive-or-failed

[Service]
Type=oneshot
StandardInput=socket
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
ExecStart=systemctl --user restart myapp.service
